          "TwilioSid": {
            "title": "Twiliosid",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "UndeliveredContactNumber": {
            "title": "Undelivered Contact Number",
            "description": "For a group-conversation message, the specific participant number whose relay leg failed, resolved from Twilio's per-recipient onDeliveryUpdated ParticipantSid (PRO-6630/PRO-6632) since the message row's own ContactNumber can't name one recipient out of several. Unset for a 1:1 message, where ContactNumber already identifies the recipient, and unset if the participant lookup failed.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "UndeliveredContactNumbers": {
            "title": "Undelivered Contact Numbers",
            "description": "For a group-conversation message, every participant leg that is CURRENTLY known-failed, by number -- the per-recipient state the PRO-7304 failure alert renders from, since a group send's single Status can only ever describe one aggregate outcome and UndeliveredContactNumber (singular) only ever named the most recently-resolved failure. Index-aligned with UndeliveredParticipantSids (entry i failed as participant i). A NEW failing participant is appended; the SAME participant later correcting to a success (PRO-5002's shape, not a second person's independent failure) removes that entry instead of leaving it stuck forever (PRO-7304 round 3 -- this list is NOT append-only despite an earlier round of this same ticket documenting it that way). Populated only via the onDeliveryUpdated group-delivery path (crud.message.update_status resolve_as_group_delivery=True); unset for a 1:1 message and for a clean group delivery with no failures at all.\n\nAn ENTRY may be None: the leg is known-failed but Twilio's participant lookup could not resolve its number. The entry is still recorded, because dropping it would leave that leg with no UndeliveredParticipantSids entry either, and its own later correction could then never be matched -- pinning the row at partiallydelivered forever with nothing able to clear it (ironhide, PR #875 round 7). Consumers rendering this list must skip None entries; the count of failed LEGS is the list length, the count of NAMEABLE ones is smaller.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "UndeliveredParticipantSids": {
            "title": "Undelivered Participant Sids",
            "description": "Twilio ParticipantSid for each entry in UndeliveredContactNumbers, same index. The identity that lets update_status tell a same-participant DLR correction (PRO-5002: this exact leg corrected itself, remove it) apart from a second, independent participant's receipt (PRO-7304: two different people, two different facts, neither erases the other) -- Status and ContactNumber alone can't distinguish those. Backend-internal: not meant for the frontend to render, only to let this field's sibling list self-correct accurately. An entry can itself be None (a legacy row seeded from the pre-sid-tracking singular UndeliveredContactNumber field, or the Twilio Participant lookup failed) -- update_status's correction matching requires an actual sid on BOTH sides, so a None entry here can never be mistaken for a match against an incoming None sid.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "UserId": {
            "title": "User Id",
            "description": "Id of the app user",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "UserNumber": {
            "title": "Number for the app user",
            "description": "Number with a leading +1",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "WebhookUrlStatus": {
            "title": "Webhookurlstatus",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "WhatsAppContentSid": {
            "title": "WhatsApp Content Sid",
            "description": "Server-resolved Twilio Content SID for a template send. Not client-settable.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "WhatsAppContentVariables": {
            "title": "WhatsApp Content Variables",
            "description": "Server-resolved positional {'1': value, ...} substitutions for a template send. Not client-settable.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "WhatsAppTemplateId": {
            "title": "WhatsApp Template Id",
            "description": "An approved WhatsAppTemplate to send this message with, bypassing the 24h session window",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "MessageId"
        ]
      },
